    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that creating an owner return a `displayName` formatted exactly as `'LastName, FirstName'` from the stored names. I made two changes following the project's standard Spring/OpenAPI conventions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema. The `OwnerDto` is code-generated from this spec, so this gives it a `displayName` field, getter, and setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(displayName(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, backed by a `default` helper that returns `lastName + \", \" + firstName` from the stored `Owner`.\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response now serializes `displayName` as `\"LastName, FirstName\"`, and `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` passes. Full `./mvnw test` reports **BUILD SUCCESS** with 0 failures/errors.",
